## Which refreshers do you need? (a 3-minute self-check)

Try to answer each question in your head. If you hesitate, the linked refresher is worth 15–30 minutes **before** (or while) reading the Pass-2 chapters that need it. You can also just start, and follow 🔁 links as they appear.

| If this question makes you hesitate… | …read this refresher | Used heavily in |
|---|---|---|
| Solve $\frac{dy}{dt} = -\frac{y}{\tau}$ and $\frac{dy}{dt} = \frac{y_{eq}-y}{\tau}$. What do the solutions look like? | [RM1 — ODEs for MRI](refreshers/RM1_ODEs_for_MRI.ipynb) | A2 Bloch equation, D1 contrast |
| Why does $e^{-i\omega t}$ describe a *clockwise* rotation, and what happens when you add 1000 unit phasors with random phases? | [RM2 — Complex numbers & rotations](refreshers/RM2_Complex_Numbers_and_Rotations.ipynb) | A2, D2/D3 ($T_2^*$, echoes) |
| How does the integral $F(k)=\int f(x)e^{-i2\pi kx}dx$ relate to `np.fft.fft`, and why do we need `fftshift`? | [RM3 — Continuous FT ↔ DFT](refreshers/RM3_Continuous_FT_and_DFT.ipynb) | C2, F1–F3 |
| What does a *shift* in $x$ do to the Fourier transform? What is the transform of a product? | [RM4 — Fourier properties](refreshers/RM4_Fourier_Properties.ipynb) | E2 slice offsets, I1 PSF, H3 partial Fourier |
| What is the FT of a rectangle? What happens to the spectrum when you sample a signal? | [RM5 — Fourier pairs & sampling](refreshers/RM5_Fourier_Pairs_and_Sampling.ipynb) | E1 RF pulses, G1 FOV & resolution, I2 artifacts |
| In the 2D FFT of a photo, where are the edges and where is the overall brightness? | [RM6 — 2D Fourier & images](refreshers/RM6_2D_Fourier_and_Images.ipynb) | F2 k-space |
| What magnetic field does a current loop produce, and why is a long solenoid's field uniform inside? | [RP1 — Magnetism from currents](refreshers/RP1_Magnetism_from_Currents.ipynb) | B2–B4 hardware |
| Why does a rotating magnet near a coil produce a voltage? What is an LC resonance? | [RP2 — Induction & RF](refreshers/RP2_Induction_and_RF.ipynb) | B5 RF chain, C2 signal, G2 SNR |
| Why does a spinning top *precess* instead of falling over? | [RP3 — Precession & torque](refreshers/RP3_Precession_and_Torque.ipynb) | A1, A2 |
| What is a nuclear spin, and why are only ~10 in a million protons "useful" at 3 T? | [RP4 — Spin & thermal statistics](refreshers/RP4_Spin_and_Thermal_Statistics.ipynb) | A1, G2 |

